\end{equation}
For simulation, we make the following two assumptions:
\begin{assumption} Only the 1st (target) satellite has RWs to control its attitude, and the 2nd (chaser) satellite does not. Then, the electromagnetic torque on the chaser is only controlled, and the uncontrollable electromagnetic torque due to angular momentum conservation acts on the target, which RW attenuates based on Eq.~(\ref{reaction_wheel}).
\end{assumption}
\begin{assumption}
The current amplitudes on the 1st (target) satellite are predetermined based on arbitrary constant $c_{\mathrm{amp}0}=3$, the relative position, and the random coefficients to ensure regularity of matrix in Eq.~(\ref{decentralized_current_allocation}) before the decentralized current allocation in Eq.~(\ref{decentralized_current_allocation}), i.e.,
