\subsection{Comparison with SOTA Methods}
We conduct comparison with SOTA methods.
As shown in Table \ref{tab:comparison}, our framework demonstrates superior performance: 1) Thanks to the pose-aware visual processor and semantic alignment pool, our CSR model achieves WER scores of 0.030 for normal-hearing cuers and 0.254 for hearing-impaired cuers, significantly outperforming previous SOTA CSR methods; 2) Leveraging the strong understanding capabilities of CSR, our UniCUE model also achieves lower WER scores. Additionally, our UniCUE surpasses others in FAD, LSE-D, and LSE-C metrics, showcasing high-quality, temporally aligned, and expressive speech generation.

\subsection{Ablation Studies}
To systematically validate the contribution of each component, we conduct controlled ablation studies on both normal-hearing and hearing-impaired test data.
