The key findings are analyzed as follows:
\textbf{1) Unified Training Paradigm.} 
Compared with the single CSV2S baseline, our UniCUE reduces WER by 62\% (0.056 \textit{vs.} 0.258) for normal-hearing cuers and 22.7\% (0.293 \textit{vs.} 0.379) for hearing-impaired groups. 
This verifies that transferring fine-grained semantic knowledge from CSR to CSV2S through shared visual representation learning effectively alleviates the challenge of complex semantic correlation.
