\textbf{2) Visual Processor Design.} 
We analyze the impact of pose-aware visual processor by comparing CSR\textsuperscript{‡}+TTS \textit{vs.} CSR+TTS and CSV2S\textsuperscript{†} \textit{vs.} CSV2S. Models relying solely on raw video features exhibit suboptimal performance due to their limited capacity to capture fine-grained motion patterns. This suggests that unprocessed video frames contain substantial interference from redundant visual information. By integrating pose estimation features as supplementary inputs, the model gains enhanced fine-grained awareness of motions, leading to significant improvements in both CSR and CSV2S tasks.
Furthermore, the pose features enhances model robustness against inter-cuer variability. As illustrated in Figure \ref{fig:cuer}, our model maintains consistent performance across six normal-hearing cuers when speaking same linguistic content, demonstrating the importance of introducing pose-aware information.
\textbf{3) Semantic Alignment Mechanism.}
Disabling the semantic alignment pool (CSR\textsuperscript{††}+TTS) weakens the pose-text correlation, causing 17.9\% relative WER increase (0.030 \textit{vs.} 0.125). The contrastive alignment loss enforces spatiotemporal consistency between visual cues and CS phonemes, which is particularly beneficial for accurate semantic content.
\textbf{4) VPA Mechanism.} 
Removing the VPA (UniCUE\textsuperscript{*}) results in an 85.7\% degradation in FAD (1.749 \textit{vs.} 2.219), indicating that the cross-attention-based VPA effectively bridges the representation gap by adaptively selecting critical visual-semantic cues relevant to speech characteristics through learnable query interaction.  
\textbf{5) Qualitative Analysis.} 
To more comprehensively demonstrate the advantages of our unified framework UniCUE, we also provide qualitative comparison of CSR+TTS, CSV2S, and UniCUE. As shown in Figure \ref{fig:ablation}, UniCUE achieves more accurate temporal alignment with the ground truth, indicating its superior ability to capture temporal dynamics within the visual modality. In contrast, CSR and CSV2S exhibit noticeable temporal drift.



