\caption{Network optimization. All edges here correspond to bipartite secret key rate $r=1$. (a): The initial ring-like network of 6 nodes gives the conference key rate $r_{\rm conf}=6/5$. If we are allowed to add one link (edge), then which of two links marked as red dashed edges is it better to choose? The optimal choice is to add the link $(1,4)$.  (b): If we are  allowed to add one more link, which of three marked options is optimal? The optimal solution is to add $(2,6)$ or $(3,6)$ because the addition of the link $(1,5)$ leads to a triangle bottleneck structure, see the text.
