\section{Dataset Details}
\label{sec:dataset_details}
MMAU~\cite{sakshi2024mmau} is a novel benchmark designed to evaluate the capabilities of large-scale multimodal audio understanding models. 
MMAU consists of $10,000$ carefully curated audio-question-answer pairs, covering three major audio domains: speech, sound, and music. 
These questions involve both information extraction and reasoning tasks, spanning $27$ distinct skills that challenge models to demonstrate advanced audio perception and domain-specific reasoning abilities. 
The dataset is divided into two parts: the Test-mini set, containing $1,000$ questions, and the main Test set, which includes $9,000$ questions. 
As the Test set is not open-sourced, we used the Test-mini set for our experiments. 
The Test-mini set reflects the same task distribution as the main Test set, and thus serves as a reliable evaluation set for reliable methods. 

