An \emph{optimal solution} refers to a set of points $y_0,\dots,y_{\opt-1}$ on the boundary such that they form a partition of $\partial P$ into $\opt$ visible intervals, i.e. $[y_i,y_{i+1}]\in\Fc$ and $\bigcup_{i=0}^{\opt} [y_i,y_{i+1}] = \partial P$ and $\opt$ is minimal with this property. 
Next, we show that any \emph{greedy step}, $(x,\Gsc(x)]$, always contains at least one point from every optimal solution (similar to Lemma 2.3 in~\cite{circle_cover_arc_minimization_1984_LEE1984109}). 

