\begin{proof}
    Let $(x_i)_{i=0}^\infty$ be the greedy sequence starting at $x$. Assume that $k > 1$ is minimal such that $x_{k+1} \in [x_0, x_1]$. Thus this candidate solution uses $k+1$ guards.

