\section{Neural Networks into Pre-Closed Regional Format}
\label{sec:nn2pwl}
Given a ReLU--TId neural network $N$ for which $\mathcal{L}_N = \{ L_0,\ldots,L_\Lambda \}$, we provide an algorithm to translate it into a tuple $\Xi_N = \tuple{\Xi_1,\ldots,\Xi_{|L_\Lambda|}}$, where each $\Xi_k$, $k\in\{1,\ldots,|L_\Lambda|\}$, is the codification for a rational McNaughton function in pre-closed regional format, which we will show to be the function computed by $N$ through the path to its $k$-th output node. Each $\Xi_k$ is a set of pairs $\tuple{p,\Omega}$, where $p$ is a linear piece and $\Omega$ is its associated region.

