The results of the automated search were refined by the inclusion and exclusion criteria presented in Tables  \ref{table:Inclusion_Criteria} and~\ref{table:Exclusion_Criteria}.  
As the stop criterion for the analysis, we selected having three consecutive pages, where all items are irrelevant wrt. specified inclusion and exclusion criteria. We reached it on page 25 of the Google Scholar results (pages have been sorted by relevance). 
This phase was conducted in two steps: 
\begin{enumerate}
   \item %\textbf{Step 3.1:} 
   Preliminary refinement, where we analysed only the title and the abstract of the paper, based on the above criteria. As application of IC2 and especially EC3 might be limited when only the title and abstract are considered, a further step of refinement is necessary. 
   \item %\textbf{Step 3.2:} 
