\begin{proof}
Fix $i\in\{-t,\ldots, k\}$ and assume $i\ge 0$. For $i<0$, the proof is symmetric. 
Since $p_i\in\Strip_i$ and by the
definition of the lower barrier, $y_+(\lb(p_i))<y(p_i)<y_+(\Strip_i)$. 
If $y_-(\lb(p_i))>y_-(\Strip_i)$, since $\lb(p_i)\in\mathcal{R}_s$ and
