Otherwise, we have $\ub(p_i)\in\mathcal{R}_s$.
Since $p_i\in\Strip_i$ and 
by definition of the upper barrier, we have $y_-(\ub(p_i))>y(p_i)>y_-(\Strip_i)$.
Since
$y_+(\Strip_i)\le\min\{y_+(R'): R'\in\mathcal{R}_s\mbox{ and } y_-(R')>y_-(\Strip_i)\}$,
it follows that
$y_+(\Strip_i)\le y_+(\ub(p_i))$.
\end{proof}


