%\vspace{-1mm}
\section{Conclusions}

This paper addresses the challenges of target sensing in MIMO-radar systems with limited-size antenna arrays at an AP. While existing approaches using DFT-based methods can handle multiple targets but suffer from low angular resolution, and MUSIC-based techniques offer high resolution but are limited by antenna count constraints, our proposed solution bridges this gap. We introduce a novel algorithm that first separates targets in the delay or Doppler domains before performing DoA estimation, enabling effective use of MUSIC even with small antenna arrays. The algorithm incorporates an innovative fusion methodology to mitigate sidelobe interference effects, thereby enhancing DoA estimation accuracy. Through numerical simulations, we demonstrated the superior performance of our approach in achieving high-resolution target sensing in distributed MIMO-ISAC systems.

