\begin{abstract}
The integrated Sachs-Wolfe (ISW) effect is a property of the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB), in which photons from the CMB are gravitationally redshifted, causing the anisotropies in the CMB. An intriguing question is whether one can infer the gravitational perturbations from the ISW effect observed near the Earth. In this work, we address the question using a tomographic reconstruction approach, similar to X-ray CT reconstruction in medical imaging. We develop the mathematical analysis for the stable inversion of the X-ray transform in the cosmological setting. %Also, we conduct a numerical study %for partial data problems to investigate the spectral properties of the forward model. 
In addition, we provide a numerical study of reconstruction methods, thereby demonstrating the feasibility and potential of the tomography method. 
\end{abstract}
